module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.Cardinality.LocalOrder.KernelCount.Tables

/-!
# First-row witnesses for the binary products

The rows are indexed by the eleven-bit mask, with the least significant bit
selecting the first matrix. The input matrices and bit convention are those of
`KernelCount.Tables` (ATLAS `J4G1-max1W1`). These are untrusted witness data;
`Certificates` checks the recurrence, bounds, and a left inverse in the kernel.
Balanced decision trees keep kernel reduction of individual lookups inexpensive.
Only indices below 2048 are used by the certificates.
-/

